# Protected core: do not touch

## Context

`app/src/store.ts` (the dispatch/notify engine) and `app/src/types.ts` (core
types + the `Action` union) are load-bearing: the reducer, action creators,
selectors, and tests all depend on their exact shapes. Careless edits ripple
through the whole app.

## Rule

- NEVER modify `app/src/store.ts`. Feature work belongs in `reducer.ts`,
  `actions.ts`, and `selectors.ts`.
- Do not change `app/src/types.ts` except for the two sanctioned extensions:
  adding a new variant to the `Action` union, or adding a field to a domain
  type when the task explicitly requires it.
- Any other change to these two files requires explicit approval from the user
  FIRST — ask before editing, and say which lines you want to change and why.
- NEVER rewrite, reformat, or "clean up" these files as a side effect of
  another task.

## How to verify

1. `git diff app/src/store.ts` is empty in the final change set.
2. `git diff app/src/types.ts` shows only additions (new `Action` variant /
   new field), no removed or rewritten lines.
3. `cd app && npm test` — the seeded `store.test.ts` still passes untouched.
